SUMMARY:Free Friday night movie @ Innis Town Hall. Deliverance
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n🏕️
  Free Movie Night: Deliverance — A Classic That Will Make You Think Twic
 e About Camping!\n\nLooking for something a little darker this Halloween s
 eason? Join us Friday\, October 23 at Innis Town Hall for a FREE screening
  of the 1972 survival thriller Deliverance. 🎬\n\n📍 Innis Town Hall\n
 2 Sussex Avenue\, Toronto\n🎬 Movie starts: 7:10 PM\n⏱️ Runtime: 109
  minutes\n\n🌲 About the Movie\n\nFour friends head into the wilderness 
 for a canoe trip down a remote river before a proposed dam changes the lan
 dscape forever.\n\nWhat begins as an adventurous weekend quickly becomes a
  fight for survival as they encounter increasingly dangerous circumstances
  deep in the backcountry.\n\nStarring Jon Voight\, Burt Reynolds\, Ned Bea
 tty and Ronny Cox\, Deliverance is one of the most famous—and unsettling
 —survival movies ever made.\n\n🎥 Watch the trailer on YouTube:\n"Watc
 h the Deliverance (1972) Trailer" ([https://www.youtube.com/results?search
 _query=Deliverance+1972+official+trailer](https://www.youtube.com/results?
 search_query=Deliverance+1972+official+trailer))\n\n👋 Meet Nick\n\nMeet
  Nick in the lobby before the movie.\nI'll have a Meetup sign so you can e
 asily find me.\n\n💰 FREE EVENT!\n\nThere are NO charges or fees for thi
 s Meetup.\n\nPlease respect your RSVP—if you RSVP\, please make every ef
 fort to attend.\n\nNot sure about your schedule yet? That's okay! You can 
 simply just show up if you're unsure whether you'll be able to make it. No
  pressure to RSVP.\n\nCome out\, meet some fellow movie fans\, and experie
 nce one of the most iconic—and unforgettable—films of the 1970s. 🏕
 ️🎬\n\nJust remember: this is probably not the movie to watch right be
 fore planning your next canoe trip. 😬
