SUMMARY:🍂 Fall Walk: Rouge National Urban Park and  Picnic🌳
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🍂
 🌳 Fall Walk: Rouge National Urban Park 🌳🍁\n\n### A Real Hike\, Be
 autiful Fall Colours & a Picnic Together\n\nWant to get out of the city wi
 thout actually leaving Toronto?\n\n**Rouge National Urban Park** is Canada
 's only urban national park — and one of the most popular hikes we do.\n
 Once you get onto the trail\, it can be hard to believe you're still in To
 ronto. Forest paths\, rolling hills\, changing leaves\, and quiet stretche
 s of wilderness make this feel much more like a trip outside the city than
  a walk through it.\nAnd fall is one of the best times to experience it.\n
 \nThis is **a real hike**\, though. There are some hills and ups and downs
 \, so it isn't the best choice if you're looking for an easy\, flat walk.\
 nBut if you're up for the challenge\, there's something satisfying about r
 eaching the end knowing you did it together.\nAnd then we'll have a picnic
 . 🧺\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](
 https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🥾 What
  We'll Do\n\nWe'll meet at **Don Mills Station** and take the 85C bus toge
 ther toward Rouge National Urban Park.\nOnce we arrive\, we'll begin our h
 ike through the park.\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Hike through forest and o
 pen spaces 🌳\n* Enjoy the fall colours 🍂\n* Navigate the hills and c
 hanging terrain\n* Take in some beautiful views\n* Stop for a short break 
 along the route\n* Finish at the Park's Welcome Centre\n* Have a **30–40
  minute group picnic** afterward 🧺\n\nThe hike takes approximately **2
 ½ hours**\, plus a short break.\nAfterward\, we'll take some time to rela
 x\, eat\, and enjoy each other's company.\n\n***\n\n## 🍁 Fall Weather &
  Expectations\n\nThis is a **moderately challenging hike**\, not a casual 
 stroll.\nThere are hills\, uneven sections\, and some ups and downs\, so g
 ood walking or hiking shoes are important.\nPlease come prepared for typic
 al fall weather and bring enough water for the hike.\n\nIf you're comforta
 ble walking for a couple of hours and handling some elevation changes\, yo
 u'll be fine.\nIf you're looking for something completely flat and easy\, 
 **this probably isn't the walk for you.**\n\n***\n\n## 🚌 Meetup Details
 \n\n### 🚇 By TTC\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Don Mills Station — on 
 the platform for the **85C bus**\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n
 ⏰ **Meetup Time:** **9:45 AM**\n🚌 **Bus Leaves:** **10:06 AM sharp**\
 nI'll wait for the bus\, but if you miss it\, **you won't be able to join 
 the group afterward.**\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n\n### 🚗
  By Car\n\nParking is **not available at our TTC meeting point.**\n\nIf yo
 u're driving\, please park at the **Toronto Zoo** and walk to the **Park's
  Welcome Centre (the house)**.\n🚗 **Car Meetup Time:** 11:00 AM\n\nWe m
 ay be a few minutes late arriving\, depending on the bus and traffic.\n\n*
 **\n\n## 🧺 The Picnic\n\nAfter the hike\, we'll have a **30–40 minute
  group picnic** at the end.\nPlease bring something small to share — not
 hing too large or heavy. The goal is simply to have something to eat toget
 her after the hike.\n🥪 Sandwiches\n🍎 Fruit\n🍪 Snacks\n🥤 Drinks
 \nWhatever is easy to carry and share is perfect.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup
  Details at a Glance\n\n🥾 **Hike:** Approximately 2½ hours + short bre
 ak\n🧺 **Picnic:** 30–40 minutes\n🏁 **End Point:** Park's Welcome C
 entre\n💲 **Meetup Fee:** $5 cash or e-transfer\n📧 **mathewmaclean@ho
 tmail.com**\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n🥾 Good walki
 ng shoes or hiking shoes\n🥪 A snack\n🧺 Something small to share for 
 the picnic\n🧥 A fall jacket or layers\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For
 ?\n\nThis hike is great for:\n\n* People who enjoy a little challenge\n* A
 nyone who wants to explore Rouge National Urban Park\n* People who love fa
 ll colours 🍂\n* Hikers looking for a social outing\n* Anyone comfortabl
 e walking hills and uneven terrain\n* People who want to meet others while
  getting outside\n\nThis isn't the easiest walk we do.\n**But sometimes th
 e harder walks are the ones you remember.**\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahea
 d of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.
 \nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed\,
  so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer:
  Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email **torontomoviesand
 outings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the hike.**\n**Stay for the picnic.**\
 n**Leave with a new connection — and maybe a new friend.** 🍂💛
