SUMMARY:🍂🌿 NEW FALL WALK: Discover Biidaasige Park 🌿🍂
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🍂
 🌿 **NEW FALL WALK: Discover Biidaasige Park** 🌿🍂\n\n### A Brand-N
 ew Toronto Park\, Fall Colours & Waterfront Trails\n\nWe're trying somethi
 ng **new**!\n\nJoin us for our first group walk to **Biidaasige Park**\, o
 ne of the newest and most ambitious parks in Toronto. Opened as part of th
 e massive transformation of the Port Lands\, the park sits on **Ookwemin M
 inising**\, Toronto's new island where the Don River meets Lake Ontario.\n
 \nThis isn't a walk we've done before\, which makes it a little more excit
 ing. We'll spend much of the afternoon actually **exploring the park rathe
 r than rushing through it** — following its trails\, enjoying the waterf
 ront\, taking in the fall scenery\, and stopping along the way to apprecia
 te the new landscape.\nThe park is enormous\, with more than **50 acres al
 ready open** and more sections being added as the Port Lands transformatio
 n continues.\n\nThere are curated trails and paths\, viewpoints\, natural 
 areas\, and places to get down closer to the new Don River.\nAnd because w
 e're doing this in the fall\, we'll get to experience the park at a comple
 tely different time of year — cooler air\, changing leaves\, open skies\
 , and fewer summer crowds. 🍂\n\nWe'll meet at the **Young Centre in the
  Distillery District** simply because it's an easy and convenient meeting 
 point before we head toward the park. We won't be spending the day touring
  the Distillery District — **the park is the destination.**\n\n📲 **Do
 n't Forget to join our WhatsApp Group – [\\[CLICK HERE!\\]](http://xn--%
 5Bclick%20here!%5D(%20join%20our%20whatsapp%20group-cu832c:%20Click%20here
 %20to%20join)/)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ **What We'll Do**\n\nWe'll me
 et outside the **Young Centre for the Performing Arts** and make our way t
 oward Biidaasige Park.\nOnce we reach the park\, we'll slow things down an
 d spend about **90 minutes exploring the trails and waterfront**.\nAlong t
 he way we'll:\n\n* 🍂 Enjoy the fall colours\n* 🌿 Explore the park's 
 trails and green spaces\n* 🌊 Walk along the new waterfront landscape\n*
  📸 Stop for photos and scenic views\n* 🌳 Explore the natural areas a
 round the new Don River\n* 🌆 Take in views toward the Toronto skyline a
 nd Toronto Islands\n* 🚶‍♂️ Enjoy plenty of time to walk and talk 
 with the group\n\nThe walk itself will be approximately **2 hours**\, but 
 we're not trying to race through it.\n**This is about experiencing the par
 k.**\nIt's our first time doing this walk\, so we'll take our time and act
 ually enjoy discovering what has been created here.\n\n***\n\n## 🌊 **Wh
 y Biidaasige Park?**\n\nBiidaasige Park is part of one of the biggest tran
 sformations Toronto has seen in decades.\nThe new Don River was created as
  part of the Port Lands Flood Protection project\, transforming former ind
 ustrial land into a new river valley\, wetlands\, parkland and public spac
 es.\n\nThe first phase of Biidaasige Park opened in July 2025.\nThe park i
 ncludes **accessible trails\, cycling paths\, river access\, wetlands\, vi
 ewpoints and waterfront promenades**\, with views toward the Toronto Islan
 ds\, Inner Harbour and skyline.\n\nAnd there's something particularly fun 
 about visiting a place that is still **brand new**.\nWe're not revisiting 
 an old Toronto favourite.\n**We're discovering somewhere new together.**\n
 \n***\n\n## 🍺 **After the Walk: The Keating Channel Pub & Grill**\n\nAf
 ter exploring the park\, we'll head over to **The Keating Channel Pub & Gr
 ill** for lunch.\nThe pub sits right on the Keating Channel and has been a
  local fixture in the area for more than 20 years. After years of Port Lan
 ds construction made the neighbourhood difficult to reach\, the transforma
 tion of the area has brought new life and new visitors back to the waterfr
 ont.\nIt's a nice way to finish the day: **a brand-new park followed by on
 e of the neighbourhood's old survivors.**\nLunch is optional\, but everyon
 e is welcome to join us.\n\n***\n\n## 🍂 **Fall Weather & Expectations**
 \n\nThis is a **social urban walk**\, not a difficult hike.\nWe'll be walk
 ing for approximately two hours\, including our time exploring the park\, 
 so you should be comfortable being on your feet for that length of time.\n
 Please dress for typical Toronto fall weather. The waterfront can be coole
 r and windier than other parts of the city\, so a warm layer is a good ide
 a.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 **Meetup Details**\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Outsi
 de the **Young Centre for the Performing Arts**\, 50 Tank House Lane\, in 
 the Distillery District. Young Centre for the Performing Arts\n🫎 **Look
  for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time: 11:00 AM sharp**\nI will on
 ly wait **5 minutes**.\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **End
  Point:** The Keating Channel Pub & Grill\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ **Meetup Fe
 e**\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.c
 om**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows us to continue organizin
 g walks and events throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 **What to Bring**
 \n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥪 A snack\n🧥 Weather
 -appropriate clothing\n📸 Your phone or camera for photos\n\n***\n\n## 
 🌈 **Who Is This For?**\n\nThis walk is great for:\n\n* People who enjoy
  discovering new places in Toronto\n* Anyone who likes parks and waterfron
 t trails\n* People who want a relaxed social walk\n* Anyone interested in 
 seeing Toronto's newest public spaces\n* People who enjoy exploring somewh
 ere they've never been before\n* Anyone who wants to spend a fall day outs
 ide with good people\n\nThe park may be new.\n**The idea is the same: come
  out\, walk with us\, and meet some people along the way.**\n\n***\n\n📲
  **You're welcome to RSVP ahead of time — or just show up on the day if 
 you're unsure about your schedule.**\nSometimes things happen and events m
 ay need to be cancelled or changed\, so please keep an eye on the event pa
 ge for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the ev
 ent wall or email:\n📧 **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come
  discover a new park.**\n**Stay for the fall colours.**\n**Stay a little l
 onger for lunch and friendship.** 🍂🌿🍺
