SUMMARY:👻 Ghost Tour of Old Toronto🌙!
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 👻 
 Ghost Tour of Old Toronto 🌙\n\n### Haunted Hotels\, Dark History & The 
 Ghosts of Downtown\n\nToronto has a long history — and some of it is con
 siderably darker than the history books make it sound.\n\nJoin us for an e
 vening walk through **Old Toronto**\, where we'll uncover stories of haunt
 ed hotels\, gruesome executions\, mysterious deaths\, and some of the stra
 nger legends that have become part of the city's history.\nWe'll walk thro
 ugh the downtown core as the city settles into the evening\, stopping alon
 g the way for stories about the ghosts\, tragedies\, and unusual events co
 nnected to the streets and buildings around us.\nAnd yes\, we'll even expl
 ore **why Toronto has a long-standing fear of clowns.** 🤡👻\n\nThis i
 sn't simply a walk through downtown.\nIt's a **curated storytelling experi
 ence** that looks at some of Toronto's history from a decidedly darker per
 spective.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HER
 E](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 👻 W
 hat We'll Explore\n\nWe'll begin outside the **Royal York Hotel** and make
  our way through Old Toronto toward the **Hockey Hall of Fame**.\nAlong th
 e way\, we'll hear stories about:\n\n* 🤡 **Why Toronto doesn't like clo
 wns**\n* 🏨 **The ghosts of downtown's historic hotels**\n* 💀 **Grues
 ome executions and forgotten tragedies**\n* 🔫 **A deadly reminder of wh
 y you should never play with guns**\n* 👻 **Restless spirits and strange
  encounters**\n* 🕯️ And much\, much more…\n\nWe'll remain outside t
 hroughout the experience and **will not be entering the buildings**.\n\n**
 *\n\n## 🕯️ A Little About the Experience\n\nThis is one of our **cura
 ted ghost walks**\, rather than a regular social walk.\nI've researched th
 e stories\, developed the route\, and brought together some of the strange
 r pieces of Toronto's history to create an evening experience that is part
  history\, part ghost story\, and part “what the hell happened here?”\
 nYou don't have to believe in ghosts.\n**You just have to enjoy a good sto
 ry.** 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** I
 n front of the **Royal York Hotel**\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**
 \n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **6:30 PM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes**.\
 n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🚶‍♂️ **Pace:** Steady wa
 lking pace\n🏁 **End Point:** **Hockey Hall of Fame**\n\n***\n\n## 🎟
 ️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$10 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmacle
 an@hotmail.com**\nThis is a **curated ghost-walking experience**\, rather 
 than one of our regular social walks. The route\, stories\, and history ha
 ve been researched and brought together specifically for this experience.\
 nThe fee helps support the time and work that goes into creating these wal
 ks.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n
 🧥 Weather-appropriate clothing\n💧 Water\n📱 Your phone for photos\
 n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis experience is great for:\n\n* 
 👻 People who love ghost stories\n* 🏙️ Anyone interested in Toronto
 's history\n* 🕯️ Fans of the strange and unexplained\n* 🤡 People b
 rave enough to learn about Toronto's clown problem\n* 🚶 Anyone looking 
 for something different to do in the evening\n* 😂 People who enjoy bein
 g a little creeped out without taking it too seriously\n\n***\n\n**Come fo
 r the history.**\n**Stay for the ghost stories.**\n**Leave looking at Old 
 Toronto a little differently.** 👻🌙\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:** You're we
 lcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure ab
 out your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be canc
 elled or changed\, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\
 n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email:\n
 📧 **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the history.**\
 n**Stay for the ghost stories.**\n**Leave looking at Old Toronto a little 
 differently.** 👻🌙
